    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d314">

                <pb facs="0425" n="337" xml:id="pg337"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-08-06"><hi rendition="#italic">August 6,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Replying to Mr. Choate’s telegram of the 3d instant Mr. Hay states that, as the
                    Department is not sufficiently advised of all the facts and circumstances
                    connected with the sinking of the <hi rendition="#italic">Knight Commander</hi>,
                    it is not prepared to express an opinion on the case, nor can it say that, in
                    case of imperative necessity, a prize may not be lawfully destroyed by a
                    belligerent captor. It is deemed inadvisable for the Department to express an
                    opinion concerning the volunteer fleet, as that would involve a proper
                    construction of a treaty to which the United States is not a party. In regard to
                    the general subject of the right of search for contraband and the mode of
                    visitation for that purpose, it seems to be quite well regulated by
                    international law, and an opinion could only be expressed on a concrete
                    question.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
